From 7711b03c28b91329f87919f2fcd91f019fa7e6a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Kwabena W. Agyeman" <kwagyeman@openmv.io>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:21:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] stm32/boards/ARDUINO_NICLA_VISION: Lower the QSPI clock to
 66MHz.

At 100MHz the QSPI flash on the Nicla Vision isn't reliable under
sustained erase and program.  In a loop of 4KiB erases and writes on the
ROMFS partition the controller wedges within a few passes: a status
register read (RDSR) starts, BUSY stays set and TCF never comes, so
qspi_read_cmd() spins forever inside mp_spiflash_wait_sr() with no IRQ
involved (setting CR.ABORT un-wedges it).  Some writes also read back
wrong.  The other boards that run QSPI at 100MHz (GIGA, Portenta H7)
don't do this; the Nicla runs the MCU from a 1.8V rail.

Divide the 200MHz kernel clock by 3 instead of 2.

Tested on a Nicla Vision with the same build and only the prescaler
changed, each pass erasing and writing 242 4KiB blocks with a
memory-mapped readback: at 100MHz it wedged or failed a readback within
7 passes in every run; at 66MHz 160 of 160 passes were clean, and at
50MHz 40 of 40.

Signed-off-by: Kwabena W. Agyeman <kwagyeman@openmv.io>
---
 ports/stm32/boards/ARDUINO_NICLA_VISION/mpconfigboard.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ports/stm32/boards/ARDUINO_NICLA_VISION/mpconfigboard.h b/ports/stm32/boards/ARDUINO_NICLA_VISION/mpconfigboard.h
index 399fa20..65526f1 100644
--- a/ports/stm32/boards/ARDUINO_NICLA_VISION/mpconfigboard.h
+++ b/ports/stm32/boards/ARDUINO_NICLA_VISION/mpconfigboard.h
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ void NICLAV_board_osc_enable(int enable);
 
 #if !MICROPY_HW_ENABLE_INTERNAL_FLASH_STORAGE
 // QSPI flash for storage
-#define MICROPY_HW_QSPI_PRESCALER           (2) // 100MHz
+#define MICROPY_HW_QSPI_PRESCALER           (3) // 66MHz (100MHz is unreliable on this board)
 #define MICROPY_HW_QSPIFLASH_SIZE_BITS_LOG2 (27)
 // Reserve 4MiB for romfs and 1MiB for WiFi/BT firmware.
 #define MICROPY_HW_SPIFLASH_SIZE_BITS       (88 * 1024 * 1024)
